# Feature Architecture - ToolkitSync

## System Architecture Impact
`ToolkitSync` bridges local database contexts (`NSManagedObjectContext` or SwiftData `ModelContext`) with target REST servers.

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant App as Host App
    participant DB as CoreData / SwiftData
    participant Sync as ToolkitSync Engine
    participant Auth as ToolkitAuth Manager
    participant Net as ToolkitNetworking
    participant Bus as Core EventBus

    App->>DB: Mutates Entity (@SyncedModel)
    DB-->>Sync: Trigger change detection (mark dirty fields)
    App->>Sync: syncNow()
    Sync->>Auth: Request fresh access token
    Auth-->>Sync: Returns Token
    Sync->>Net: POST /sync/delta (Serialized delta payload)
    alt Conflict Occurred
        Net-->>Sync: Return 409 Conflict Response
        Sync->>Sync: Run pluggable ConflictStrategy
        Sync->>Bus: Publish SyncConflictEvent
    else Sync Success
        Net-->>Sync: Return 200 OK (Clean state metadata)
        Sync->>DB: Clear dirty markings, update syncHash
    end
```

## Key Components
- **`SyncedModelMacro`**: A Swift compiler plugin that auto-generates tracking properties.
- **`SyncEngine`**: Orchestrates serializing delta records and coordinates background sync loops.
- **`SyncConflictResolver`**: Evaluates conflict strategies on mismatched records.
- **`BackgroundSyncScheduler`**: Registers task identifier with iOS `BGSystem` frameworks.
